    crm:P129i_is_subject_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/diary/1902-03/document/71> ;
    crm:P183i_has_representation <https://ids.lib.harvard.edu/ids/iiif/493310000/full/full/0/default.jpg> ;
    rdf:value """hope that the Fat Lady was perhaps beginning to lose her hold over him. But she said she would  never let him go.
I read Donna Laura’s chapter on Fogazzaro, and found it rather dull and futile, but perjured my soul out in praises of it in the evening. Tu l’as voulu - I might reply if she reproached me, for she and her sister put me in a position where I could do nothing but praise. Donna Carmelita told me that a word of adverse criticism would make her sister take to her bed. They are the most awful, tactless, bad-mannered, embarrassing people I ever came across. But they aren’t bores, so I prefer them greatly to il Casto Naso! """^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 71 ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:part_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/resource/diary/1902-03> .

